  "title": "US Solar Module Imports Plunge 78% as Domestic Manufacturing Expands: Crux",
  "summary": "The value of crystalline silicon (c-Si) solar module imports into the U.S. fell 78% between the first half (1H) of 2024 and 1H 2026, as trade enforcement measures and domestic manufacturing incentives reshaped the country’s solar supply chain, according to a white paper by Crux.Module import value fell from $7.6 billion in 1H 2024 to $1.7 billion in 1H1 2026. Southeast Asian countries covered by U.S. trade measures accounted for 86% of c-Si module import customs value in 1H 2024, but their share dropped to less than 2% two years later.",
